---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Roy Li for Richmond">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Richmond deserves practical leadership</div>
          <h1>A city hall that sees every family.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Roy Li is building a campaign for residents who want safer streets, disciplined spending, honest planning, and a stronger voice for the communities that keep Richmond moving.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/volunteer/">Join the campaign</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="/platform/">Read the platform</a>
          </div>
          <p class="lang-note">中文信息请见 <a href="/zh/">中文版页面</a>。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-card">
          <div class="portrait-placeholder"></div>
          <h2>This campaign is not about one person winning.</h2>
          <p>It is about Richmond families, taxpayers, homeowners, renters, small businesses, and new Canadians feeling that their vote is finally a vote for themselves.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What this campaign stands for</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">The message is simple: representation must become results. Richmond needs leadership that listens carefully, spends responsibly, and governs in the open.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Safe, livable neighbourhoods</h3><p>Public safety, traffic, parks, and basic city services should be treated as everyday quality-of-life priorities.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Respect for taxpayers</h3><p>City Hall should be disciplined with public money and clear about what residents receive for every tax dollar.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Transparent governance</h3><p>Residents deserve decisions they can understand, meetings they can follow, and representatives who answer directly.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <div class="quote">“When you vote for Roy, it should feel like you are voting for yourself.”</div>
      <div class="list">
        <div class="list-item"><strong>For families</strong> A city that protects daily life: schools, safety, parks, mobility, and affordability.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>For small businesses</strong> A city that understands permits, parking, local customers, and the cost of delay.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>For new Canadians</strong> A city where representation is not symbolic — it produces access, respect, and real influence.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta">
        <div>
          <h2>Help build the campaign.</h2>
          <p>Volunteer, host a conversation, request a lawn sign, or tell us what Richmond needs to hear.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button primary" href="/volunteer/">Get involved</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
